msgid "Policy templates"
msgstr "Policy templates"

msgid "Gives a starting point to an organisation that has no security policy yet: ready-to-adapt templates written by the project, each with its sections and the Annex A controls it covers. The templates follow the requirements of the standard in our own words."
msgstr "Gives a starting point to an organisation that has no security policy yet: ready-to-adapt templates written by the project, each with its sections and the Annex A controls it covers. The templates follow the requirements of the standard in our own words."

msgid "Fill in the name of the organisation, the information security manager and the review period, tick the templates you need, then import them. Each one becomes a new draft policy, linked by section to the controls of the Statement of Applicability. Adapt the text to your practice, then have it approved: nothing is approved automatically and no existing policy is replaced."
msgstr "Fill in the name of the organisation, the information security manager and the review period, tick the templates you need, then import them. Each one becomes a new draft policy, linked by section to the controls of the Statement of Applicability. Adapt the text to your practice, then have it approved: nothing is approved automatically and no existing policy is replaced."

msgid "Tick at least one template."
msgstr "Tick at least one template."

msgid "Each template is written by the project in its own words, without copying the text of the standard, and is offered under the %s licence: you may adapt it freely. Importing a template creates a new draft policy; review it, adapt it to your practice and have it approved like any other policy."
msgstr "Each template is written by the project in its own words, without copying the text of the standard, and is offered under the %s licence: you may adapt it freely. Importing a template creates a new draft policy; review it, adapt it to your practice and have it approved like any other policy."

msgid "Language of the templates:"
msgstr "Language of the templates:"

msgid "Values inserted into the text"
msgstr "Values inserted into the text"

msgid "Organisation name"
msgstr "Organisation name"

msgid "Information security manager"
msgstr "Information security manager"

msgid "Review period (months)"
msgstr "Review period (months)"

msgid "A value left empty is replaced by a reminder in square brackets, to be completed in the policy. The information security manager becomes the owner of the policies created."
msgstr "A value left empty is replaced by a reminder in square brackets, to be completed in the policy. The information security manager becomes the owner of the policies created."

msgid "Sections"
msgstr "Sections"

msgid "Already imported"
msgstr "Already imported"

msgid "Create the ticked policies as drafts"
msgstr "Create the ticked policies as drafts"

msgid "%1$d draft policy created, with %2$d links to the Statement of Applicability. Adapt it, then have it approved."
msgid_plural "%1$d draft policies created, with %2$d links to the Statement of Applicability. Adapt them, then have them approved."
msgstr[0] "%1$d draft policy created, with %2$d links to the Statement of Applicability. Adapt it, then have it approved."
msgstr[1] "%1$d draft policies created, with %2$d links to the Statement of Applicability. Adapt them, then have them approved."
